Treat the token in a DHT get_peers reply as optional

BEP 5 says a get_peers reply carries a token, and aria2 rejects the whole
message when it is absent. The live bootstrap routers (dht.transmissionbt.com,
dht.libtorrent.org) answer bootstrap queries with a node list and no token, so
every reply is discarded as "Malformed DHT message. Missing token" and a fresh
routing table can never bootstrap - which breaks peer discovery for magnet
links that have no working tracker.

Accept a missing token and pass an empty one instead. Nothing downstream needs
it for the node list or the peer list: DHTPeerLookupTask::getPeers already
skips announcing to nodes whose stored token is empty ("Token is empty for
ID:..."), so a tokenless router is used for lookups and never announced to.

Verified against dht.transmissionbt.com: before the patch, 5 replies rejected
and 0 peers found; after it, the lookup proceeds and magnet metadata arrives.

--- a/src/DHTMessageFactoryImpl.cc
+++ b/src/DHTMessageFactoryImpl.cc
@@ -445,9 +445,14 @@ DHTMessageFactoryImpl::createGetPeersReplyMessage(
       }
     }
   }
-  const String* token = getString(rDict, DHTGetPeersReplyMessage::TOKEN);
+  // Bootstrap routers reply with nodes but no token. Dropping the message
+  // would leave an empty routing table unable to bootstrap, so the token is
+  // optional here; DHTPeerLookupTask skips announcing to tokenless nodes.
+  const String* token =
+      downcast<String>(rDict->get(DHTGetPeersReplyMessage::TOKEN));
   return createGetPeersReplyMessage(remoteNode, std::move(nodes),
-                                    std::move(peers), token->s(),
+                                    std::move(peers),
+                                    token ? token->s() : std::string(),
                                     transactionID);
 }

